      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Major Tourist Islands & Landmarks"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "In 2018, Ross Island was renamed Netaji Subhash Chandra Bose Dweep, Neil Island became Shaheed Dweep, and Havelock Island was renamed Swaraj Dweep.",
        "Radhanagar Beach on Swaraj Dweep (Havelock) holds Blue Flag certification and is a primary international tourist attraction.",
        "Restricted Area Permits (RAP) and Protected Area Permits (PAP) regulate foreign and domestic visitor access to ecologically sensitive island zones.",
        "Adventure and eco-tourism initiatives focus heavily on coral reef conservation, scuba diving, and sustainable mangrove exploration."
      ],
      "id": "o9pl39n"
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Sustainable island tourism balances ecological preservation of delicate coral ecosystems with historical and adventure landmark access.",
      "id": "s9enz18"
    },
